 "notes": "Headline result: bounds on ultra-light hidden-photon DM (HPDM) from requiring DM-induced gas heating not exceed the HI radiative cooling rate in the gas-rich dwarf Leo T. Curve is the black solid 'Leo T gas temp.' line in Fig. 2 (figs/ULDP.pdf), extracted as a vector figure (piecewise-linear, V-shaped with minimum g~6.4e-11 at m~1.4e-12 eV, the Leo T plasma frequency). x-axis m_V in eV, y-axis kinetic mixing g, which equals canonical chi (paper Lagrangian couples e J.(A + g A~), so g is the kinetic mixing to leading order); reported directly. Points clipped to plotted frame [1e-19,1e-9] eV; paper quotes validity 1e-23<m<1e-10 eV. All DM assumed to be hidden photons; heating uses the spatially-varying Leo T Burkert DM halo profile (Ref.[94], Fig.1), so no single DM density value applies (dm_density_assumed=null). Conservative energy-balance limit, not a stated statistical CL.",
